# REQUIRES: python-api, hdf5, h5py
# The one wait of a Python simulation for the frames on their own
# thread (D400, #113), Inputs/python_frame_writer.py: waters in
# a rhombic dodecahedron at constant pressure on the CPU, whose barostat
# changes the cell and its tilts, through parts that end between frames and
# at frames, checkpoints, changes of the reporters, frames of the state
# with velocities in H5MD, a commit of a cell, the close of the reporters,
# and the end of a simulation. With each write held back by 500 ms
# (MDIR_FRAME_WRITE_DELAY), longer than the 10 steps between two frames on
# the CPU, the file holds every frame of a part when the part returns, and
# the energies, the trajectories, and the checkpoints with the frames they
# count are those of the same script without the hold, byte for byte (HDF5
# by content). The end of a part is the one point that waits: the calls
# between parts come after it.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_writer.py %S/Inputs/triclinic %t/plain | FileCheck %s
# RUN: env MDIR_FRAME_WRITE_DELAY=500 %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_writer.py %S/Inputs/triclinic %t/held | FileCheck %s
# RUN: cmp %t/plain/run.dat %t/held/run.dat
# RUN: cmp %t/plain/run.dcd %t/held/run.dcd
# RUN: cmp %t/plain/moved.dcd %t/held/moved.dcd
# RUN: %h5md_python %S/Inputs/compare_h5_contents.py %t/plain/state.h5md %t/held/state.h5md | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAME
# RUN: %h5md_python %S/Inputs/compare_h5_contents.py %t/plain/last.h5md %t/held/last.h5md | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAME
# RUN: mdir checkpoint %t/plain/first.h5 %t/held/first.h5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STATES
# RUN: mdir checkpoint %t/plain/second.h5 %t/held/second.h5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STATES
# RUN: mdir checkpoint %t/held/first.h5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FIRST
# RUN: mdir checkpoint %t/held/second.h5 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SECOND

# CHECK: frames after step 35 3
# CHECK: frames after step 60 6
# CHECK: frames after step 100 10
# CHECK: committed a cell 1.001 times the one of step 175
# CHECK: done at step 220
# SAME: identical contents
# STATES: the states are identical
# FIRST: trajectory: run.dcd, 10 frames
# SECOND: trajectory: moved.dcd, 5 frames
